 "result": "`Tessel.async_to_sync` (`src/tessel/app.py:1079`) uses `asgiref.sync.async_to_sync`. It imports it lazily inside the method and returns `asgiref_async_to_sync(func)`.\n\n- If `asgiref` isn't installed, it raises `RuntimeError` telling you to install Tessel with the `async` extra.\n- The method is meant to be overridden to change how async code is run synchronously.\n- `ensure_sync` (around L1075) calls it for coroutine functions, which is how async views get run.",
